WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:06.439
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and since the
Terminus people on Walking Dead have been

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:11.049
outed as Cannibals I wanted to do a bonus
video explaining the Hunters in the Comics

00:00:11.049 --> 00:00:12.740
since they’re very similar.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:17.120
It’s also possible they could be doing some
scenes from the Tainted Meat storyline in

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.120
Episode 2.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:22.230
So I’ll explain those when I post my Review
tonight.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:24.170
New Round of the Giveaway starts when I post
that too.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:27.349
All you have to do to enter is be a subscriber
and leave a comment.

00:00:27.349 --> 00:00:32.570
The show also cast two new characters that
I’ll explain at the end of this video.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:37.079
So careful for spoilers through the premiere,
but as mentioned.

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:39.980
The Hunters are a group of cannibals in the
comics.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:45.110
They’re not exactly like the Termites but
they appear in issues 61 through 66, so if

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:49.760
you want to read along in the comics you should
check out Volume 11 Fear the Hunters, it combines

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.700
all those.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:59.390
Their leader is named Chris and they’re
a small band that preys on people instead

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:02.769
of hunting animals because they think people
are easier to catch.

00:01:02.769 --> 00:01:07.530
As a group they might be a little worse than
the Termites, they ate their children.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:11.960
The Termites we know ate each other, if you
remember the kill floor in episode 1.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:15.240
Scott Gimple confirmed that the body being
chopped up here was Gareth’s brother.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:18.360
Still somehow eating your own children sounds
worse than eating your adult brother.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:21.350
So the Termites aren’t quite as bad as the
Hunters.

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:26.960
In the comics, Rick and the Survivors run
into the Hunters on their way to Washington

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:30.350
DC, they don’t say exactly where they are
on the map.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:35.900
But it’s somewhere between Atlanta and DC
in the middle of nowhere, like the woods we

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:37.300
see around Father Gabriel’s church here.

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.910
It’s also around this time that they run
into Father Gabriel in the comics, so just

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:41.920
more evidence that they’ll do some Hunter-Related
moment on the show.

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:44.259
Chris and his Hunters start chasing down the
survivors and it turns into a hunt or be hunted

00:01:44.259 --> 00:01:45.259
arc.

00:01:45.259 --> 00:01:46.880
Andrew J West, the actor who plays Gareth
is very similar to Chris.

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:47.880
The jackets they’re wearing even look alike.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:50.140
After the finale last year he was upgraded
to cast Regular.

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:54.670
They only do things like that if they intend
to feature a character in most of the episodes

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:55.920
during a season.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:02.340
So if you’ve read the comics, I think they
will change some things from the Hunters storyline.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:05.200
It’s possible that Rick and the Survivors
could capture Gareth and he would become their

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.200
prisoner.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:10.580
Michonne has her katana here, so it’s possible
she takes it off the body of a dead termite.

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:14.800
Father Gabriel’s church is one of the big
locations from the comics, and from the way

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:15.800
it looks here.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:18.950
It’s possible the Survivors could use it
as bait for the Termites.

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:19.950
Hunt or Be Hunted.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:24.690
I think they’ve even been using that language
in the promos.

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:29.610
Scott Gimple already said that there would
be villains this season to rival the Governor.

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:38.040
He didn’t say there would be another governor
character, he just said their would be people

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:40.290
or a person that’s just as evil.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:44.270
I don’t think he was talking about Gareth,
since he’s kind of a cannibal hipster.

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:45.850
And Hipsters are mostly harmless.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:49.390
Feel free to make all the evil hipster jokes
you want.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:55.510
I do think they will adapt some of the Hunter
moments but I think Gareth is a much bigger

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:56.510
character than Chris.

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:59.590
If you have read the comics, just please use
spoiler tags if you’re going to talk about

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:02.430
what happens at the end of their storyline.

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:08.250
The whole arc in the comics mirrors a lot
of the changes I think we’re going to see

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:10.580
in Rick’s character.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:16.410
Since he’s the conscience of the group,
naturally everyone else starts to adapt with

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:17.410
him.

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:18.670
Hunt or Be Hunted.

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:22.350
So they all slowly learn to be Hunters.

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:25.950
Not cannibal hunters like the Hunters group.

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:28.460
But you get the idea.

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:35.510
They just stop being such easy prey for people
like the Termites.

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:46.790
The whole arc of The Hunters in the comics
is fairly self contained, but it’s a crucible

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:50.120
that everyone walks out of looking way more
badass.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:54.640
If you remember Rick at the end of season
4 when he bit into Joe’s Neck and they killed

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:55.640
all the Claimers.

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:57.380
It’s just the natural progression of that.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.520
This is going to be a big season for Andrew
Lincoln.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:01.420
It makes me wonder how long he’ll stay with
the show.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:06.050
He’s not getting paid crazy money compared
to say the Big Bang Theory actors, but I think

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:09.720
he could stay till the main show goes off
the air.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:17.180
I don’t expect the actors from the main
show to appear on the companion show.

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:20.840
That’s just what they’re calling the spin
off that’s going to start next year.

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:23.810
Which reminds me, two new characters were
just cast.

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:25.310
On the main show that is.

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:26.310
For Season 5.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:28.530
Alexandra Breckenridge is going to play someone
named Samantha.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:32.420
That’s not someone from the comics, but
just like Gareth, she could be like someone

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:34.000
from the comics with a different name.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.800
Her character description reads: attractive,
strong, smart, charming and articulate woman

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:37.870
with a vulnerable side.

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:40.810
She's a mother with a bohemian spirit, and
a talented artist

00:04:40.810 --> 00:05:53.190
She’s not going to appear for a while.

00:05:53.190 --> 00:06:36.140
They 
just cast her in the last week and they’ve

00:06:36.140 --> 00:06:37.500
already shot the first half of the season.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:47.230
So we probably won’t see her till next year.

00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:51.020
You might have seen her on American Horror
Story, she usually plays some sort of temptress

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:53.120
with really gruesome consequences.

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:58.530
But that doesn’t necessarily mean she’s
going to be having sex with Rick or anything.

00:06:58.530 --> 00:07:02.700
If they do make it to Washington DC by next
year, it’s possible she could be one of

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:08.600
the new characters in the Alexandria Safe
Zone.

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:13.740
They are casting another character named Donna
right now, but they haven’t picked an actress

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:14.740
yet.

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:17.040
Supposedly Kate Burton from Scandal is their
top pick.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:22.850
The funny part about this is that in the comics,
Donna was the mother of Ben and Billy.

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:25.460
On the show they gave their storyline to Lizzie
and Mika.

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:29.870
The other new character we haven’t seen
yet is Noah, he’s being played by Tyler

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:32.330
James Williams from everybody hates chris.

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:35.080
He’s not someone from the comics either.

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:38.231
It sounds like he’ll be in at least a few
episodes, so I don’t think we’ll meet

00:07:38.231 --> 00:07:42.100
him till after the Survivors leave Father
Gabriel’s Church.

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:46.590
So I will be posting my episode 2 review tonight
after the episode airs.

